evan: Quick flag - hit a deterministic edge in the node sample app where a fast reconnect during auth rotation produces mis-ordered fragments and occasional duplicate final tokens. Repro + short log below.

mai: Minimal repro? Browser too?

evan: Node-only so far. Repro harness: open, close quickly, reconnect with jitter. After ~300 loops we get JSON parse errors.

```
// fast-reconnect-poc.js
const {EventSource} = require('eventsource');
const url = process.env.URL;
let i=0;
setInterval(()=>{
  const es = new EventSource(url);
  setTimeout(()=> es.close(), 90);
  if(++i>400) process.exit(0);
}, 120 + Math.random()*80);
```

harper: Trimmed trace: partial chunk "{\"choices\":[{\"text\":\"...\"\"", then auth rotate -> new conn emits fragment from different response, then leftover of previous fragment arrives -> parser emits in wrong order -> duplicate closing bracket / extra final token.

mai: Sounds like parser instance swap + old socket tail. Did you try the SDK's buffering or hold-until-delimiter options?

evan: Buffering reduces freq but doesn't eliminate it. Key problem: current reconnect path creates a new parser and starts consuming immediately, no attempt to reconcile leftover bytes from previous socket.

harper: Short-term mitigation ideas: (1) server can send explicit "flush" event on auth rotate; (2) client adopt ephemeral monotonic per-fragment header (x-frag-seq) and drop fragments with seq <= lastSeen when reconnect detected; (3) add tiny drain-window (configurable) before new parser consumes.

mai: I prefer seq-drop + CI e2e that randomizes auth rotate timing. Drain window could add small latency, so feature-flag it.

evan: I'll open a small PR in sampleapp with a `drop_stale_fragments_on_reconnect` flag (default false) and a repro job under devex/sampleapp/repro/fast-reconnect-poc.js. Will attach logs. Assigning @mai and @harper.

sdk-bot: Created ticket <https://tracker.redwood.ai/RED-9010|RED-9010> "node sampleapp: fast reconnect -> fragment reordering" and attached minimal logs.

infra-bot: Note: this is more visible when TCP delayed ACKs or lingering CLOSE_WAIT occurs; adding a short note to infra runbook.

harper: Long-term: parser should be able to reassemble fragments across reconnects when resume token/Last-Event-Id present. That requires protocol work (per-fragment ids + resume mapping). Track in RED-9010.

mai: Thanks evan  please include benchmark notes in PR showing tail latency impact if you try drain-window. Will review today. :thumbsup:
